WEBVTT

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:32.860
Hi, I'm glad you could join me today.

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:34.640
Today let's do something a little bit different.

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:37.090
Today I'm gonna start with a canvas that's just,

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:39.450
it's dry, doesn't have any magic white on it.

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:41.450
So I'll have them graphically run all the colors

00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:44.080
across your screen that you need to do this painting,

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:45.690
and let's get started.

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:48.610
I'm gonna start today with a two and a half inch brush.

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:50.110
I'm gonna put a little paint thinner on it

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:52.570
and go right into some Burnt Umber.

00:00:52.570 --> 00:00:56.060
Very thin paint, and just a small, small amount.

00:00:56.060 --> 00:00:58.930
And I'm just gonna put a little wash up here on the canvas.

00:00:58.930 --> 00:01:00.000
This is just Burnt Umber.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.550
or a number, and just wash the canvas.

00:01:04.550 --> 00:01:10.380
Just applying a small, small amount of color.

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:17.390
Okay, there we are.

00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:21.640
Now really scrubbing that paint into the fabric.

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:24.100
Okay, take a tiny bit more of the thinner,

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:27.810
and I'm gonna go right into a little bit of phthalo blue.

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:30.000
Didn't clean the brush, didn't clean the brush.

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:38.570
It takes very little of this blue, it's a very strong color.

00:01:38.570 --> 00:01:42.420
And we'll just throw a little happy wash up here.

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:44.120
And by wash, I mean the paint is so thin

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:45.930
it's almost like water.

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:47.930
This will dry in just a couple of minutes.

00:01:47.930 --> 00:01:49.730
It'll dry even faster here in the studio

00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:52.990
because we have all the lights on the canvas at home.

00:01:52.990 --> 00:01:55.730
You might want to give it a few minutes to dry a little bit

00:01:55.730 --> 00:01:59.380
so it's not so runny, but very thin, very light.

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:07.030
Okay, and that gives us a little background color.

00:02:07.030 --> 00:02:13.450
That easy.

00:02:13.450 --> 00:02:16.060
All right, let's lay the brush down,

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:18.940
and today, let's have some fun with the knife.

00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:22.420
I'm gonna go right in here and get some titanium white.

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:25.730
Let's just start playing like,

00:02:25.730 --> 00:02:30.000
maybe there's some little cloud shapes that just sort of float

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:32.300
in the sky up here.

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:35.500
And this old knife will do fantastic things.

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:37.440
Fantastic things, but you gotta turn it loose

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:39.300
and let it go.

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:43.530
Gotta let it go.

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:46.690
Be brave with it.

00:02:46.690 --> 00:02:49.460
See, now it's picking up that color underneath.

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:50.960
And you can make all kinds of beautiful

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:53.590
little cloud effects just using the knife.

00:02:53.590 --> 00:02:56.190
Just using the knife.

00:02:56.190 --> 00:02:59.150
Maybe it goes right on off the canvas there.

00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:00.000
This is your sky.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.320
so you put things where you want 'em.

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:10.500
Let 'em happen, let 'em happen.

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:12.090
And when you're painting with a knife,

00:03:12.090 --> 00:03:14.290
normally you'll probably use a little more paint

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:17.280
than you normally do, because it's thicker on the canvas.

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:18.950
It has texture when it's dry.

00:03:18.950 --> 00:03:23.490
It makes a beautiful, beautiful effect, though.

00:03:23.490 --> 00:03:26.230
Just clean that knife off,

00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:28.800
and we can just rub this a little bit,

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:30.000
and it picks up the undercut

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:33.530
It just blends the bottom of these clouds right in.

00:03:33.530 --> 00:03:37.590
All the beautiful blues and browns that we've got there.

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:42.210
And there we go.

00:03:42.210 --> 00:03:47.650
See how easy you can make a sky just, just using a knife.

00:03:47.650 --> 00:03:50.360
You don't have to have all the big fancy brushes.

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:52.780
All you need is a nice, nice knife.

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:57.340
A little practice and have some fun.

00:03:57.340 --> 00:04:00.000
Well, maybe, maybe a little bit

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:02.780
Under this beautiful little sky here,

00:04:02.780 --> 00:04:05.050
maybe there's a happy little mountain.

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:06.840
I'll take some Van Dyke brown,

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:08.780
and I'll take some Prussian blue.

00:04:08.780 --> 00:04:11.590
Good, strong, dark blue.

00:04:11.590 --> 00:04:13.030
Little bit of alizarin crimson.

00:04:13.030 --> 00:04:16.270
Just mix 'em together here.

00:04:16.270 --> 00:04:18.330
Put a little white in there.

00:04:18.330 --> 00:04:21.890
Okay, so we got blue, brown, a little crimson,

00:04:21.890 --> 00:04:23.760
and a small amount of white.

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:25.040
Okay, let's go up here.

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:28.630
Maybe, maybe, maybe, there it is.

00:04:28.630 --> 00:04:30.000
I knew there was a big old mountain lift.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.920
up here somewhere, you just have to sort of find him,

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:37.200
decide where he's at, drop him in, that's all there is to it.

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:40.810
And when these paintings are dry,

00:04:40.810 --> 00:04:44.710
they look a great deal like traditional paintings,

00:04:44.710 --> 00:04:47.050
where you would take washes and glazes

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:50.000
and all those good things.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:52.630
These paintings will give you that feeling.

00:04:52.630 --> 00:05:00.000
Okay, now just rub that right in like that, just rub it.

00:05:03.260 --> 00:05:04.880
You want this mountain to be a little bit lighter

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:07.500
down toward the horizon.

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:12.920
Rub it, let it pick up that color it's underneath.

00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:15.330
The excess paint you can just scrape off.

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:16.710
All you're looking for is that dark,

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:19.640
dark value in the canvas.

00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:30.000
There we go, little bumps and bangs in there.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:33.200
Ready? Now, let's put some highlights on this mountain.

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:34.820
Let's take, I'll tell you what,

00:05:34.820 --> 00:05:39.750
take some white, a little bit of alizarin crimson.

00:05:39.750 --> 00:05:41.510
Just a very, very small amount.

00:05:41.510 --> 00:05:42.890
We don't want to set this mountain on fire.

00:05:42.890 --> 00:05:45.700
We just want to warm it up a little bit.

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:48.230
And it's also a little easier for you to see at home.

00:05:48.230 --> 00:05:51.580
And maybe there's a little light that plays

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:53.800
right down through here.

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:57.850
Just let it strike the canvas, just like so,

00:05:57.850 --> 00:05:59.890
wherever you think the light would strike.

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:04.300
play and have fun.

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:06.960
Okay, a little bit, yep, right there.

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:11.020
There it is, there it is.

00:06:11.020 --> 00:06:16.220
A little bit, there.

00:06:16.220 --> 00:06:18.870
Just let all these things happen.

00:06:18.870 --> 00:06:21.920
Flow right out of your mind.

00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:27.290
There, there, there, there.

00:06:27.290 --> 00:06:29.830
And down to some of this color and let it pick up.

00:06:30.350 --> 00:06:33.060
together.

00:06:33.060 --> 00:06:34.920
Okay, now I'm gonna take some white,

00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:37.850
a little bit of Prussian blue mixed into it,

00:06:37.850 --> 00:06:41.760
and we'll make a little shadow type color.

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:44.100
And we'll go in here, and just here and there

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:47.850
we'll put some indications of a few shadows.

00:06:47.850 --> 00:06:50.700
I don't wanna cover up all that dark.

00:06:50.700 --> 00:06:52.630
Just here and there,

00:06:52.630 --> 00:06:54.640
a few little shadowy things happening.

00:07:00.280 --> 00:07:03.810
Very soft and very quiet when it's done.

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:05.190
Okay, maybe there's a little light strikes

00:07:05.190 --> 00:07:07.050
right out here on that peak.

00:07:07.050 --> 00:07:08.250
It's your mountain.

00:07:08.250 --> 00:07:10.550
You let light strike where you want it.

00:07:10.550 --> 00:07:14.060
That's where we want it.

00:07:14.060 --> 00:07:20.080
Little shadow right in there.

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:23.750
There's another happy little shadow.

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:27.750
Just let those little shadows just play and fall in there.

00:07:30.670 --> 00:07:37.230
Again, just blend that together

00:07:37.230 --> 00:07:41.040
so it makes it look nice and misty.

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:49.390
Easy, you can just bring that together.

00:07:49.390 --> 00:07:52.290
I'm really pushing quite hard here.

00:07:52.290 --> 00:07:55.220
I want to blend that, it's misty.

00:08:00.090 --> 00:08:03.340
Okay, tell you what, let's have a happy little

00:08:03.340 --> 00:08:04.880
foothill back here.

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:06.940
And for that, I'll use a little brown,

00:08:06.940 --> 00:08:11.790
a little sap green, put some white in it.

00:08:11.790 --> 00:08:15.220
So we got some brown, some sap green, some white.

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:16.860
And I'm gonna put into that,

00:08:16.860 --> 00:08:19.680
we'll just put a little bit of this blue.

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:21.440
Just a little blue.

00:08:21.440 --> 00:08:24.280
Maybe this is phthalo blue.

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:27.000
There, that's about what I'm looking for.

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:29.760
Okay, let's go right up here.

00:08:30.320 --> 00:08:33.590
Maybe there's a happy little foothill

00:08:33.590 --> 00:08:35.680
that lives right here.

00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:38.200
And first we'll just, still just using the knife.

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:39.460
I'm gonna just use the knife today

00:08:39.460 --> 00:08:44.080
and show you what can be done.

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:47.120
See there?

00:08:47.120 --> 00:08:50.160
Just a little indication of a little foothill back here.

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:53.800
You want it to be very soft at the bottom.

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:55.760
You need that little misty area.

00:08:55.760 --> 00:09:00.000
That's your separator, that separates.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:02.780
Now I'm gonna just keep using that same color.

00:09:02.780 --> 00:09:04.700
Maybe I'll add a small amount of blue to it,

00:09:04.700 --> 00:09:08.290
make it a little bit more into the bluish hue.

00:09:08.290 --> 00:09:09.790
Let's go right over here, maybe there's a,

00:09:09.790 --> 00:09:12.270
yep, there is, I see it.

00:09:12.270 --> 00:09:16.330
It's another little bit that comes right down.

00:09:16.330 --> 00:09:18.670
See, this is a little darker, it's a little closer to you,

00:09:18.670 --> 00:09:21.190
so it stands out a little more.

00:09:21.190 --> 00:09:23.080
See, I'm just pushing this up here and there

00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:27.390
to make it look like little trees, far, far away.

00:09:27.390 --> 00:09:30.000
As things get closer to you, you want to have more

00:09:30.030 --> 00:09:33.560
I'll add a little white so I can create some mist

00:09:33.560 --> 00:09:37.320
down here at the bottom.

00:09:37.320 --> 00:09:41.080
And as things get closer, you begin making out color.

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:45.240
You can see all kinds of little colors

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:47.030
as things get closer.

00:09:47.030 --> 00:09:50.350
So if you wanted to begin showing the least little amount

00:09:50.350 --> 00:09:53.260
of color, I'll add a tiniest little bit of cad yellow

00:09:53.260 --> 00:09:54.680
here and there.

00:09:54.680 --> 00:09:57.410
Tiniest, tiniest little bit.

00:09:57.410 --> 00:10:00.000
Just want to put an indication here and there.

00:10:01.920 --> 00:10:02.860
Just a little.

00:10:02.860 --> 00:10:03.760
It's too far away yet.

00:10:03.760 --> 00:10:06.010
Don't want a lot of detail in it.

00:10:06.010 --> 00:10:08.010
Still too far away.

00:10:09.730 --> 00:10:11.470
Maybe, maybe.

00:10:11.470 --> 00:10:12.620
Shoot.

00:10:12.620 --> 00:10:15.010
Gonna add a little more brown to that.

00:10:15.010 --> 00:10:16.600
Same color.

00:10:16.600 --> 00:10:18.810
Little brown.

00:10:18.810 --> 00:10:20.650
See, and you just keep making these colors darker

00:10:20.650 --> 00:10:22.680
as you come closer.

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:25.120
There it is.

00:10:25.120 --> 00:10:25.800
There it is.

00:10:31.310 --> 00:10:32.150
a little hill.

00:10:32.150 --> 00:10:35.310
See, you can make as many of these little hills

00:10:35.310 --> 00:10:36.410
as you want.

00:10:36.410 --> 00:10:39.470
Just decide how many hills are in your world

00:10:39.470 --> 00:10:42.040
and drop 'em in, drop 'em in.

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:46.500
You can do anything.

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:55.570
Depends the depth in the painting

00:10:55.570 --> 00:10:57.360
using nothing but a little knife.

00:11:01.790 --> 00:11:13.430
Still same old color, a lot of rubbing.

00:11:13.430 --> 00:11:16.700
That rubbing makes it very smooth.

00:11:16.700 --> 00:11:18.020
When this is done, it'll look almost like

00:11:18.020 --> 00:11:19.700
it was done with a brush, it'll be so smooth.

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:24.480
I hope, I hope, we're shooting for anyway.

00:11:24.480 --> 00:11:28.300
And it takes a lot of this blending and rubbing,

00:11:28.300 --> 00:11:30.000
and you can spend hours and hours on it.

00:11:30.640 --> 00:11:33.130
A lot of fun, a lot of fun.

00:11:33.130 --> 00:11:35.010
It's a good painting to do when you're not in a hurry

00:11:35.010 --> 00:11:42.590
and you just want to have some fun in there.

00:11:42.590 --> 00:11:44.800
Now, I want to lighten this a little,

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:48.440
so I'll add a small amount of white and blend it.

00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:11.370
I just added a little more blue, a little brown.

00:12:11.370 --> 00:12:13.270
Put some dark in here and then we can begin

00:12:13.270 --> 00:12:17.410
working on some shape and some form, play in a little.

00:12:17.410 --> 00:12:23.810
Okay, I'm gonna go right into a little bit of yellow ochre.

00:12:23.810 --> 00:12:28.120
Yellow ochre, to that I'll put a little bit of blue,

00:12:28.120 --> 00:12:30.000
a little phthalo blue into my yellow ochre.

00:12:31.720 --> 00:12:34.470
Makes a nice green, but it's not so bright and shiny,

00:12:34.470 --> 00:12:36.010
it's a dull green.

00:12:36.010 --> 00:12:37.790
Let's go back up here.

00:12:37.790 --> 00:12:40.770
Maybe you're beginning to make out detail in here.

00:12:40.770 --> 00:12:43.900
Little, little things are starting to happen.

00:12:43.900 --> 00:12:46.120
And you can vary these colors.

00:12:46.120 --> 00:12:50.180
If it's not bright enough, you can add a little yellow.

00:12:50.180 --> 00:12:52.360
Make it as bright or as dull as you want it.

00:12:52.360 --> 00:12:54.870
Just let these colors play through there.

00:13:02.490 --> 00:13:05.120
And this is an excellent painting to do to,

00:13:05.120 --> 00:13:07.720
if you have a lot of paint left on your palette,

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:10.560
'cause you can just use any old color that you have

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:13.010
and put all these things together

00:13:13.010 --> 00:13:17.230
and just make beautiful, beautiful, beautiful paintings.

00:13:17.230 --> 00:13:20.620
And you'll really make friends with your knife.

00:13:20.620 --> 00:13:22.360
You'll get to know that thing

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:25.410
just like an extension of your hand.

00:13:25.410 --> 00:13:28.310
And that's when the fun really starts.

00:13:28.310 --> 00:13:29.890
Can you maybe,

00:13:30.220 --> 00:13:32.520
Let me go back and get a little Prussian blue,

00:13:32.520 --> 00:13:35.630
little Van Dyke brown, put a little white into it,

00:13:35.630 --> 00:13:43.180
little sap green, some more brown.

00:13:43.180 --> 00:13:49.240
Now then, now then, let's go up to the canvas,

00:13:49.240 --> 00:13:52.230
maybe right in here, maybe there'll be some water,

00:13:52.230 --> 00:13:54.570
so we need a little bit of dark under here

00:13:54.570 --> 00:13:57.450
to show a reflection.

00:13:57.450 --> 00:13:59.800
Just rub some dark in here.

00:14:03.870 --> 00:14:08.800
Just rub it down some over here.

00:14:08.800 --> 00:14:15.150
I want to kill totally all of that, but most of it.

00:14:15.150 --> 00:14:21.510
Add a little bit of that thin area to show through.

00:14:21.510 --> 00:14:29.570
Give us some dark, and onto that we can add light.

00:14:30.190 --> 00:14:32.950
So I'll take some white

00:14:32.950 --> 00:14:35.160
and a little bit of an alizarin crimson.

00:14:35.160 --> 00:14:38.610
We'll get pretty here.

00:14:38.610 --> 00:14:40.900
Just a nice pinkish glow.

00:14:40.900 --> 00:14:43.510
Let's go right up in here

00:14:43.510 --> 00:14:50.090
and just lay a little of that here and there.

00:14:50.090 --> 00:14:55.320
Just let it play and have fun.

00:14:55.320 --> 00:14:56.850
These little colors just happen.

00:15:01.600 --> 00:15:15.420
here, pushing very hard right there, very hard.

00:15:15.420 --> 00:15:28.330
There's some white and a little bit of,

00:15:28.330 --> 00:15:29.860
let's go into some phthalo blue.

00:15:31.440 --> 00:15:33.270
white, phthalo blue.

00:15:33.270 --> 00:15:38.130
Across, let's go up here,

00:15:38.130 --> 00:15:42.530
and we can begin just laying some little watery looks.

00:15:42.530 --> 00:15:46.990
Right on there, just come across.

00:15:46.990 --> 00:15:48.790
Now these little lines that you're putting in,

00:15:48.790 --> 00:15:49.810
they need to be straight.

00:15:49.810 --> 00:15:51.270
If they're not straight,

00:15:51.270 --> 00:15:53.680
it's not gonna look like water.

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:56.050
They really need to be straight.

00:16:07.900 --> 00:16:11.020
Just keep going back and forth, keep them straight.

00:16:11.020 --> 00:16:20.890
Can't say that enough.

00:16:20.890 --> 00:16:24.230
This back and forth.

00:16:34.060 --> 00:16:37.780
This is just a little bit of titanium white.

00:16:37.780 --> 00:16:40.970
Just let it go across there and pick up color,

00:16:40.970 --> 00:16:44.110
let little things happen.

00:16:44.110 --> 00:16:47.860
Touch, come across, put this together.

00:17:04.920 --> 00:17:08.460
Probably sounds loud, but remember this canvas is dry.

00:17:08.460 --> 00:17:10.470
This is a dry canvas.

00:17:10.470 --> 00:17:13.550
Normally we're working with a canvas that's wet,

00:17:13.550 --> 00:17:15.270
and so you don't hear all that.

00:17:15.270 --> 00:17:17.230
The knife would just glide across there.

00:17:17.230 --> 00:17:18.430
I've got a little Van Dyke Brown,

00:17:18.430 --> 00:17:20.300
a little Burr and Umber mixed here.

00:17:20.300 --> 00:17:24.360
And we'll just put some little areas right here

00:17:24.360 --> 00:17:27.180
to make it look like where the land comes down into the water.

00:17:27.180 --> 00:17:28.640
I'm just touching the canvas.

00:17:34.220 --> 00:17:42.330
Just touching, this just sort of separates everything.

00:17:42.330 --> 00:17:54.370
A few bushes right along in here, different yellows.

00:17:54.370 --> 00:18:00.000
Clean the old knife off, maybe, maybe.

00:18:01.560 --> 00:18:03.570
Take some blue and some brown.

00:18:03.570 --> 00:18:06.150
A little sap green.

00:18:06.150 --> 00:18:09.290
Maybe, maybe, yeah, in here.

00:18:09.290 --> 00:18:12.930
Maybe there's a little peninsula that comes out here.

00:18:12.930 --> 00:18:22.630
Just lay in a basic shape, very dark, very dark.

00:18:31.470 --> 00:18:33.140
Maybe, maybe.

00:18:33.140 --> 00:18:36.480
Underneath there's a little color in the water.

00:18:36.480 --> 00:18:39.820
And some of that dark underneath.

00:18:39.820 --> 00:18:42.400
Create the illusion of a reflection.

00:18:42.400 --> 00:18:46.410
Need a reflection in there to set it down into the water.

00:18:46.410 --> 00:18:51.990
Take some little blue and some white.

00:18:51.990 --> 00:18:54.110
Just let that go across now.

00:18:54.110 --> 00:18:56.070
That easy, that easy.

00:18:56.070 --> 00:18:57.620
Gives it the impression of water.

00:19:00.510 --> 00:19:02.410
Let me just pile up a lot of,

00:19:02.410 --> 00:19:03.670
this is just all the dark colors

00:19:03.670 --> 00:19:05.140
that are laying around my palette.

00:19:05.140 --> 00:19:06.710
Let me just pick them up.

00:19:06.710 --> 00:19:10.150
Maybe there's a right here, there it is.

00:19:10.150 --> 00:19:11.850
There's a happy little tree that lives right there,

00:19:11.850 --> 00:19:13.860
and we just, a little evergreen,

00:19:13.860 --> 00:19:16.240
we'll just start right up here.

00:19:16.240 --> 00:19:27.300
Just work it back and forth, see there?

00:19:34.350 --> 00:19:36.890
a little tree that lives here.

00:19:36.890 --> 00:19:38.250
A good way to close in this corner,

00:19:38.250 --> 00:19:43.190
we'll just make it a little tree.

00:19:43.190 --> 00:19:45.550
It's also a good way to use up any old paint

00:19:45.550 --> 00:19:51.280
you got left on your palette.

00:19:51.280 --> 00:19:54.300
Just come right around like that.

00:19:54.300 --> 00:19:57.180
What the heck?

00:19:57.180 --> 00:19:58.870
Let's bring this right around.

00:20:00.730 --> 00:20:02.950
There it goes, there it goes, there it goes.

00:20:02.950 --> 00:20:08.380
It's just Van Dyke brown and Prussian blue,

00:20:08.380 --> 00:20:10.400
blizzard and crimson, just all your dark colors.

00:20:10.400 --> 00:20:12.980
Let's just throw all your dark colors in here.

00:20:12.980 --> 00:20:17.060
Snap green.

00:20:17.060 --> 00:20:20.170
Here we're just trying to fill up the rest of the canvas

00:20:20.170 --> 00:20:28.220
with nice dark color.

00:20:28.220 --> 00:20:30.000
And these paintings are, they're really adjoining

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:32.900
to do, they're a lot of fun, a lot of fun.

00:20:32.900 --> 00:20:34.500
As I say, these are the type paintings

00:20:34.500 --> 00:20:38.540
I like to spend hours and hours and hours on.

00:20:38.540 --> 00:20:40.060
These are mood paintings.

00:20:40.060 --> 00:20:42.420
If you're in a good mood, oh, you can paint

00:20:42.420 --> 00:20:45.420
some of the most beautiful, delicate things.

00:20:45.420 --> 00:20:47.720
If you're in a bad mood, if you just had an argument

00:20:47.720 --> 00:20:50.050
or somebody kicked you, these are ones

00:20:50.050 --> 00:20:51.970
you can really take out your hostilities on.

00:20:51.970 --> 00:20:58.390
Strong, strong paintings.

00:20:58.390 --> 00:20:59.640
And we've used nothing.

00:21:00.060 --> 00:21:04.530
Nothing but a knife, except we use that 2 1/2 inch brush

00:21:04.530 --> 00:21:06.890
just to put on some wash to give it some under color.

00:21:06.890 --> 00:21:09.710
And some of that color is playing through this.

00:21:09.710 --> 00:21:11.350
You still can see it, so you have areas

00:21:11.350 --> 00:21:13.850
that are very thick with paint, areas that are very thin.

00:21:13.850 --> 00:21:17.870
It makes a beautiful, beautiful composition.

00:21:17.870 --> 00:21:20.310
Maybe, now I've got a small amount of white,

00:21:20.310 --> 00:21:22.320
so I'll just take a little white

00:21:22.320 --> 00:21:24.050
and just begin rubbing it in here.

00:21:24.050 --> 00:21:26.570
See, let all these little things just happen.

00:21:26.570 --> 00:21:28.480
Just let 'em happen.

00:21:30.060 --> 00:21:38.580
Get some sap green, green in there, a little green.

00:21:38.580 --> 00:21:43.350
Just play these colors back and forth, back and forth.

00:21:43.350 --> 00:21:49.750
I want to keep this very, very dark in front.

00:21:49.750 --> 00:21:51.370
Maybe our light's coming from the right,

00:21:51.370 --> 00:21:53.630
maybe right here in this tree there's a little light

00:21:53.630 --> 00:21:55.840
striking out here on these leaves.

00:21:55.840 --> 00:21:57.230
I don't want a bunch of color.

00:21:57.230 --> 00:21:59.530
I want to keep it dark, just, just, just.

00:22:00.060 --> 00:22:01.560
So there's a little highlight.

00:22:01.560 --> 00:22:04.160
A little highlight, a little light

00:22:04.160 --> 00:22:07.840
maybe striking right here.

00:22:07.840 --> 00:22:10.380
Isn't that something?

00:22:10.380 --> 00:22:15.440
There's a little land coming.

00:22:15.440 --> 00:22:18.410
Whatever, whatever.

00:22:18.410 --> 00:22:22.120
A little highlight here, don't want too much.

00:22:22.120 --> 00:22:28.320
Okay, all kinds of little grassy things happening.

00:22:28.320 --> 00:22:30.000
You just see little touches here and there.

00:22:31.400 --> 00:22:34.170
I don't really see a lot happening.

00:22:34.170 --> 00:22:35.170
Okay, let's go over here.

00:22:35.170 --> 00:22:37.370
Maybe there's one that lives right there

00:22:37.370 --> 00:22:41.630
and comes right down.

00:22:41.630 --> 00:22:43.770
Yellow ochre, Indian yellow, cat yellow.

00:22:43.770 --> 00:22:45.710
Then I'm just mixing them all together on the knife

00:22:45.710 --> 00:22:50.000
and just letting them happen.

00:22:50.000 --> 00:22:53.380
Just whatever, whatever.

00:22:53.380 --> 00:22:54.640
Let the canvas do the work.

00:23:07.930 --> 00:23:09.490
And this is such a fun painting.

00:23:09.490 --> 00:23:13.030
I really hope you try it, I really do.

00:23:13.030 --> 00:23:16.950
I think you'll be very satisfied with it.

00:23:16.950 --> 00:23:23.000
You send me a letter and thank me for giving you this.

00:23:23.000 --> 00:23:24.690
And I'd like to hear from you.

00:23:24.690 --> 00:23:25.830
Don't get to answer all of them,

00:23:25.830 --> 00:23:30.000
but I certainly, certainly do read every single letter.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:33.490
in every one.

00:23:33.490 --> 00:23:43.310
Don't let this get too light.

00:23:43.310 --> 00:23:46.220
I want this to stay very dark

00:23:46.220 --> 00:23:49.260
so it helps create the illusion of distance.

00:23:49.260 --> 00:23:51.160
Let's go back to the other side over here a little.

00:23:51.160 --> 00:23:54.290
Here.

00:24:02.170 --> 00:24:03.710
See, and here we so often clean your knife.

00:24:03.710 --> 00:24:08.790
And you can just gently, gently bring all this together.

00:24:08.790 --> 00:24:09.630
Very light.

00:24:09.630 --> 00:24:11.130
If it's too bright for you, rub it.

00:24:11.130 --> 00:24:14.080
There's so much dark on the canvas, it'll pick it up

00:24:14.080 --> 00:24:16.120
and make all kinds of beautiful things happen.

00:24:16.120 --> 00:24:18.750
You can darken it just by rubbing it,

00:24:18.750 --> 00:24:22.470
blending it all together.

00:24:22.470 --> 00:24:24.810
As I say, this is a super, super painting

00:24:24.810 --> 00:24:29.090
to use up any paint that you have left on your palette.

00:24:29.090 --> 00:24:30.000
Super, super.

00:24:30.060 --> 00:24:33.320
Super for that.

00:24:33.320 --> 00:24:38.530
It teaches you to love color and to play with it.

00:24:38.530 --> 00:24:40.420
Okay, let's see here.

00:24:40.420 --> 00:24:48.220
I'm gonna go back and clean up that edge a little bit.

00:24:48.220 --> 00:24:50.360
Just a little water line here and there.

00:25:02.240 --> 00:25:16.580
Golly, I think we just about got us a painting going.

00:25:16.580 --> 00:25:18.640
Stick here, it lives.

00:25:18.640 --> 00:25:19.950
Let me just take your knife.

00:25:19.950 --> 00:25:24.070
Sticks are easy to make with a knife.

00:25:24.070 --> 00:25:26.730
Let me just drop in a happy little twig.

00:25:26.730 --> 00:25:27.550
Don't want it too bright.

00:25:27.550 --> 00:25:29.380
I don't want it to stand out.

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:31.920
too much, want to be very quiet.

00:25:31.920 --> 00:25:38.260
It's a dude just back here hiding in the dark.

00:25:38.260 --> 00:25:52.240
There he goes, just like so.

00:25:52.240 --> 00:25:55.960
At least a little touch of highlight so he stands out.

00:25:55.960 --> 00:25:57.080
This is just a light color.

00:25:57.080 --> 00:25:58.160
It looks like it has a little blue,

00:25:58.160 --> 00:26:00.000
and I'm really not looking for

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:02.550
specific color, this is just stuff that's left over

00:26:02.550 --> 00:26:06.170
on the palette, okay?

00:26:06.170 --> 00:26:08.870
And we can just blend him in, let him go.

00:26:08.870 --> 00:26:11.650
And I think that'll give you a good idea

00:26:11.650 --> 00:26:13.290
of how you can do a painting using

00:26:13.290 --> 00:26:15.170
nothing but your almighty knife.

00:26:15.170 --> 00:26:16.590
So on behalf of all of us here,

00:26:16.590 --> 00:26:18.500
we'd like to wish you happy painting.

00:26:18.500 --> 00:26:19.460
See you next week.
